      "writtenOn": "2024-11-06T20:59:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some people like newer guests on older hosts too ).  I define an older host to be one which does not include aosp/3323076 (for example, auto_cf_arm_64 from the Android CI on an older QAVF image).\n\nCurrently, the default in the case of a newer guest/older host would be for the batched descriptor update mechanism to be OFF.  It needs to be ON, so protocol can only actively disable it.  Hence `disableVulkanBatchedDescriptorSetUpdate` (yes, we\u0027ll need to update the guest side too).",
      "parentUuid": "a52272ab_45658df3",
      "revId": "82f7407e135b3ac14473f70252d33fcad9d7b44b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
